{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CdWYF1R6Bt94nSwc9UdiC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01WX8HRgrf8bR3ZLPFzktW4m","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/workspace/BLAST_RADIUS.md","content":"# CVE Blast Radius Analysis: axios ReDoS (CVE-2021-3749)\n\n## 1. CVE Identification\n\n- **CVE:** CVE-2021-3749\n- **Component:** `axios` (npm package, `axios/axios`)\n- **Vulnerability class:** Regular Expression Denial of Service (ReDoS)\n- **Root cause:** The `trim()` helper in `lib/utils.js` uses an inefficient regular expression to strip leading/trailing whitespace. A crafted, extremely long input string (e.g. passed through a header or URL value that flows into `trim()`) can cause catastrophic backtracking and hang the event loop.\n- **Affected versions:** `< 0.21.2`\n- **Patched version:** `0.21.2` (and all subsequent releases)\n- **Confirmed in this workspace:** The pinned mirror `/workspace/axios` is checked out at `v0.21.1`, which is inside the vulnerable range. The vulnerable code is present at:\n  - `/workspace/axios/lib/utils.js:189-191`\n    ```js\n    function trim(str) {\n      return str.replace(/^\\s*/, '').replace(/\\s*$/, '');\n    }\n    ```\n  - `package.json` confirms `\"version\": \"0.21.1\"` at `/workspace/axios/package.json:3`.\n\nThis repo is the vulnerable version itself — it is not a consumer, but it is useful as the ground-truth artifact for confirming what the bad regex/version looks like when auditing dependents.\n\n## 2. Direct Dependents (workspace repos declaring axios)\n\nTwo repos in the workspace declare `axios` directly in a manifest:\n\n| Repo | Manifest | Declared range | Path |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| grafana | `grafana-toolkit` package | `^0.26.1` | `/workspace/grafana/packages/grafana-toolkit/package.json:73` |\n| druid | `web-console` app | `^0.26.1` | `/workspace/druid/web-console/package.json:71` |\n\nBoth declared ranges (`^0.26.1`) are already well above the vulnerable `< 0.21.2` range, so **neither manifest currently permits resolving a vulnerable axios version**.\n\n## 3. Transitive Paths\n\n### Grafana\n\n- `axios` is **not** used anywhere in the actual plugin-facing runtime/SDK packages (`packages/grafana-runtime`, `packages/grafana-data`, `packages/grafana-ui`), nor in `plugins-bundled/` or `public/app/plugins/`. Searches scoped to those paths returned no hits.\n- The only place axios is used is `grafana-toolkit`, which is Grafana's **build/CLI tooling package** (not shipped to end users or loaded by dashboards). Usages found:\n  - `/workspace/grafana/packages/grafana-toolkit/src/cli/utils/githubClient.ts:1` — GitHub API client used by the plugin-scaffolding CLI\n  - `/workspace/grafana/packages/grafana-toolkit/src/cli/utils/githubRelease.ts:1`\n  - `/workspace/grafana/packages/grafana-toolkit/src/cli/tasks/plugin.ci.ts:247-248` — posts plugin CI signing/report data\n  - `/workspace/grafana/packages/grafana-toolkit/src/plugins/manifest.ts:67-70` — posts plugin manifest for signing\n  - `/workspace/grafana/packages/grafana-toolkit/src/plugins/env.ts:132-136` — fetches CircleCI artifacts\n  - `/workspace/grafana/packages/grafana-toolkit/src/cli/tasks/searchTestDataSetup.ts:1,9`\n- Grafana's own plugin-development docs (`/workspace/grafana/docs/sources/tutorials/build-a-data-source-plugin/index.md:310`) explicitly steer plugin authors toward `getBackendSrv()` (Grafana's own proxying HTTP client) instead of axios/fetch for data source plugins — so third-party Grafana plugins are not guaranteed to pull axios in via the SDK; any exposure there would come from a plugin author's own choice to add axios as a dependency, not from Grafana core.\n- Root `yarn.lock` (`/workspace/grafana/yarn.lock`) shows **two resolved axios entries**, confirming there's no vulnerable transitive pull-in anywhere in the monorepo's dependency graph:\n  - `/workspace/grafana/yarn.lock:12397-12404` — `axios@npm:^0.26.1` → resolves to **0.26.1** (this is `grafana-toolkit`'s declared dependency)\n  - `/workspace/grafana/yarn.lock:12406-12412` — `axios@npm:^0.27.2` → resolves to **0.27.2** (pulled in transitively by some other dependency elsewhere in the workspace's tooling graph, not a direct declaration in any `package.json`)\n\n### Druid\n\n- `web-console/package.json` (`/workspace/druid/web-console/package.json:71`) declares axios directly and it is used throughout the console's frontend source, not just tooling:\n  - `/workspace/druid/web-console/src/singletons/api.ts:19-29` — the console's central `Api` singleton wraps `axios.create(...)` and is the primary HTTP client for all Druid API calls made from the browser UI.\n  - `/workspace/druid/web-console/src/utils/druid-query.ts:19-20,241-244`\n  - `/workspace/druid/web-console/src/utils/query-manager.tsx:19-21,113-129`\n  - `/workspace/druid/web-console/src/views/workbench-view/query-tab/query-tab.tsx:22,197`\n  - `/workspace/druid/web-console/src/views/workbench-view/helper-query/helper-query.tsx:22`\n  - `/workspace/druid/web-console/src/helpers/execution/sql-task-execution.ts:19-20`\n  - `/workspace/druid/web-console/src/helpers/execution/general.ts:19`\n  - `/workspace/druid/web-console/src/views/sql-data-loader-view/schema-step/rollup-analysis-pane/rollup-analysis-pane.tsx:21`\n- This means Druid's blast radius is higher in *severity if it were vulnerable* (axios sits directly in the request path of the interactive SQL/query console used by operators), but as shown below the resolved version is already patched.\n- Druid also tracks the dependency in its license manifest: `/workspace/druid/licenses.yaml:5407-5415` lists `axios`, `version: 0.26.1`, `license_file_path: licenses/bin/axios.MIT` (`/workspace/druid/licenses/bin/axios.MIT`), corroborating the resolved version below.\n\n## 4. Version Analysis — Are We Actually Vulnerable?\n\n| Repo | Declared range | Resolved/locked version | Vulnerable (`< 0.21.2`)? | Evidence |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| axios (upstream mirror) | n/a | **0.21.1** | **Yes — this is the CVE-2021-3749 version** | `/workspace/axios/package.json:3`, vulnerable regex at `/workspace/axios/lib/utils.js:189-191` |\n| grafana (`grafana-toolkit`) | `^0.26.1` | **0.26.1** (resolved in lockfile) | No | `/workspace/grafana/yarn.lock:12397-12402` |\n| grafana (other transitive) | (transitive) | **0.27.2** (resolved in lockfile) | No | `/workspace/grafana/yarn.lock:12406-12411` |\n| druid (`web-console`) | `^0.26.1` | **0.26.1** (resolved in lockfile) | No | `/workspace/druid/web-console/package-lock.json:6050-6057`, corroborated by `/workspace/druid/licenses.yaml:5413` |\n\n**Conclusion: We are not currently exposed.** The only vulnerable axios version (0.21.1) present anywhere in scope is the standalone upstream mirror itself, which is not consumed by either Grafana or Druid. Both real dependents (Grafana's `grafana-toolkit` build CLI and Druid's `web-console` frontend) already pin/resolve to `axios@0.26.1` (with one additional transitive `0.27.2` in Grafana's tooling graph), all of which post-date the `0.21.2` fix for CVE-2021-3749 by a wide margin.\n\n## 5. Priority Recommendation\n\n- **No patching action required** for CVE-2021-3749 specifically — both Grafana and Druid already resolve to patched axios releases (0.26.1 / 0.27.2), well past the 0.21.2 fix line.\n- If the vulnerable `axios@0.21.1` mirror in this workspace is meant to represent a real, separately-consumed artifact (e.g. vendored into a third-party Grafana plugin outside this scan, or an unpinned range elsewhere), that dependent was not found in `/workspace/grafana` or `/workspace/druid` and should be identified before any remediation work is scheduled.\n- Longer-term hygiene: axios in Grafana is confined to `grafana-toolkit` (dev/CI tooling) and is explicitly discouraged for use inside actual plugins in Grafana's own docs — worth keeping that boundary intentional so future plugin authors don't reintroduce an unpinned axios dependency into the runtime bundle.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":55784,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":48,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f5056c17-2ece-43e4-a1b1-00986e264a1a","uuid":"04f9906d-663e-4c86-86e3-dc26a0fbdb34","timestamp":"2026-07-29T14:53:56.606Z","request_id":"req_011CdWYEz5UYdrxn7Liaru4V"}
